2026-09-27T07:57:31.2911198Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2911539Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2911841Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2912565Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2913404Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2913489Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2913971Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2914290Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2914556Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2915528Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2915760Z ================
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2915887Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2916055Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2916434Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2916644Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2916747Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2917008Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2917167Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2917305Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2991273Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2992020Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2993267Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2994385Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2994569Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2995305Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2996145Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2996583Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2997137Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2997825Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2997979Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2998311Z ========
2026-09-27T07:57:31.2998504Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3000710Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3003086Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3003471Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3004591Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3005851Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3006901Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3007938Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3008700Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3009483Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3009705Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3010102Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3010377Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3012223Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3013533Z 
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3014492Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3015353Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:57:31.3015571Z 
